@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+---
+id: task-003-make-applypatch-conform-to-rfc-6902-in-every-case-errors-included
+type: task
+title: "Make applyPatch conform to RFC 6902 in every case, errors included"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Users of `applyPatch` report that some patches they consider invalid are accepted, that some edge cases
+give unexpected results, and that a failing patch does not always behave as RFC 6902 reads. Review how
+patches are checked and applied, and make the behaviour conform to RFC 6902 in every case, errors
+included.
+
+## What was done
+
+Review of `src/index.ts` against RFC 6902 and dl-003 to dl-005. Five deviations were reproduced before any
+change was made:
+
+- A sparse patch array (`[, op]`) skipped its hole silently, so an invalid patch was accepted. Fixed:
+  the patch is read with `Array.from`, so a hole becomes an invalid element (dl-004).
+- An invalid pointer was reported only when its operation ran, as a failed operation after earlier
+  operations had run. Fixed: `path` and `from` are checked when the patch is parsed, and reported as an
+  invalid patch naming the operation index (dl-004).
+- `move` from `""` to `""` threw "cannot remove the whole document", but dl-005 says a move to the same
+  location leaves the document unchanged. Fixed: a move to the same location returns the document
+  unchanged, after the source is checked to exist.
+- Non-JSON values (`Date`, `NaN`, nested `undefined`) and operations with inherited members are accepted.
+  This extends what dl-004 treats as an invalid patch, so it is recorded as dl-006 and is not implemented
+  yet.
+
+Tests: `test/apply-patch.test.ts` gained four red-first tests (sparse hole, invalid pointer before any
+operation, invalid `from` pointer, move of the whole document to itself). They failed before the change.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test`: 76 of 76 pass (72 before, 4 new).
+- `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` (TypeScript 5, strict mode, installed outside the repo): no errors.
+
+## Open
+
+- dl-006 (plain JSON data) is submitted and waits for approval. Its implementation is not started.
